1
00:00:21,365 --> 00:00:24,603
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:25,342 --> 00:00:30,900
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

3
00:00:31,975 --> 00:00:37,326
A few miscellaneous issues to close with, scattered around.

4
00:00:38,185 --> 00:00:42,088
We'll starts with Bilal Ibn Rabah رضي الله عنه.

5
00:00:43,101 --> 00:00:50,442
When the Khalifah(خليفه) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was recruiting fighters

6
00:00:51,128 --> 00:01:00,353
and spreading them to Iraq and Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) to call the people to Islam and to fight in the path of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

7
00:01:01,177 --> 00:01:04,738
Bilal(بلال) was watching all of this and his heart was aching.

8
00:01:05,592 --> 00:01:12,870
So he goes to the Khalifah(خليفه) and then he tells him: O, successor of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

9
00:01:13,501 --> 00:01:18,825
If you have freed me, because you want me to be near you

10
00:01:19,803 --> 00:01:26,301
and prevent me from doing what I would love to do, then I'm going to stay besides you.

11
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:32,905
But if the reason why you freed me, is for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ alone,

12
00:01:33,693 --> 00:01:37,357
and you're gonna allow me to make my own decisions

13
00:01:37,382 --> 00:01:41,462
and choose what is better for me in this life and the afterlife,

14
00:01:42,779 --> 00:01:47,574
then please allow me to go and fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

15
00:01:49,344 --> 00:01:54,360
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he freed Bilal(بلال) for the sake of Allah definitely.

16
00:01:56,065 --> 00:01:58,473
But Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه loved Bilal(بلال),

17
00:01:59,470 --> 00:02:04,021
and he wanted them to be next to him and he wanted them to be with him, they were very close.

18
00:02:05,495 --> 00:02:11,090
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: No! I have freed you for the sake of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

19
00:02:11,115 --> 00:02:16,743
And I'll read exactly what the response of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was. He said:

20
00:02:17,424 --> 00:02:22,490
اَمَّا إذَا كان هَواك في الجهاد فلم أكن لآمُركَ بِالْمَقام

21
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:31,545
إنَّمَا كُنْت أُرِيْدُ كَ لِى لْآذانِ وإنِّي لَأجِدُوْلِي فِراقِكَ  وحشَ يا بلال فما بُدَّ مِنَ التَفَرقْ

22
00:02:31,862 --> 00:02:34,987
فُرقَتًا ذالك بعدها أبَدًا حتىَّ يَومُ البَعث

23
00:02:35,674 --> 00:02:42,942
فعمل عمَلًا صالحًا يا بلال يكون ذادك من الدنيا ويزكِّركَ الله به ما حييت

24
00:02:43,958 --> 00:02:46,582
يَحسن لك به الثواب إذَ التوفيت

25
00:02:47,278 --> 00:02:49,315
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

26
00:02:50,099 --> 00:02:54,835
If your heart is attached to Jihad(جهاد), that's what you want to do.

27
00:02:55,562 --> 00:02:57,388
Then I'm not going to prevent you from doing that.

28
00:02:58,055 --> 00:03:00,627
But the reason why, I wanted you to stay.?

29
00:03:01,069 --> 00:03:04,482
Is to make Adhan(آذَان) and because I will miss you.

30
00:03:04,924 --> 00:03:08,268
However, no doubt one day we will be separated.

31
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:13,338
And it will be a permanent separation and we'll only meet on the Day of Judgment, again.

32
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:20,308
So if we must part and go, our different ways.

33
00:03:21,420 --> 00:03:25,778
Then O Bilal(بلال) I advise you to do good deeds, it will be

34
00:03:26,235 --> 00:03:27,387
ذادك من الدنيا

35
00:03:27,411 --> 00:03:34,349
It will be your food in this world, and Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will record it, for you.

36
00:03:35,492 --> 00:03:36,888
 So Bilal رضي الله عنه said:

37
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:40,427
جزاك الله من وليٌ النِعمة وَأخٌى فِي الإسلام خَيْرَا

38
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:43,918
May Allah reward you for your favors on me.

39
00:03:44,465 --> 00:03:49,209
And then he went out with Saeed Bin Aamir(سعيد بن عامر) to join the armies in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

40
00:03:51,684 --> 00:03:56,791
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه wanted Bilal(بلال) to stay with him in Madina to make Adhan(آذَان).

41
00:03:56,979 --> 00:04:01,996
But Bilal رضي الله عنه did not want to make Adhan(آذَان) for anyone after Rasool Allah ﷺ.

42
00:04:03,561 --> 00:04:05,412
After Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away,

43
00:04:05,771 --> 00:04:11,737
Bilal رضي الله عنه did not want to make Adhan(آذَان) for another Imam(اِمَام).

44
00:04:13,391 --> 00:04:16,114
He was the Muazzin(مؤذن) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

45
00:04:16,938 --> 00:04:20,140
and he wanted to remain the Muazzin(مؤذن) of Rasool Allah ﷺ

46
00:04:20,164 --> 00:04:23,268
and not to be the Muazzin(مؤذن) of anyone after him.

47
00:04:24,894 --> 00:04:28,126
And he made his request to Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق)

48
00:04:28,181 --> 00:04:31,984
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: If that's what you want to do, then you're free to leave

49
00:04:32,271 --> 00:04:38,138
Bilal Ibn Rabah(بلال إبن رباح) left and he never came back to see Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

50
00:04:38,163 --> 00:04:41,095
because Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) passed away, shortly after that.

51
00:04:42,486 --> 00:04:55,010
Another incident, the recruits for Jihad(جهاد) from the South, would come into Madina and they would gather there,

52
00:04:55,653 --> 00:04:56,828
 "ثُمَّ يَعقد الراياة"

53
00:04:56,852 --> 00:05:04,492
And then he would appoint them to their specific armies and give them their banners.

54
00:05:05,281 --> 00:05:08,997
So the meeting place, the congregating place was Madina.

55
00:05:11,567 --> 00:05:16,358
So you'd have all of these tribesmen coming into Madina

56
00:05:17,653 --> 00:05:20,233
and their character was different than the people of Madina. See!

57
00:05:21,108 --> 00:05:26,874
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, who spend time with Rasool Allah ﷺ, you could see it in their manners

58
00:05:27,977 --> 00:05:29,999
their conduct, their behavior is different,

59
00:05:30,023 --> 00:05:32,011
Rasool Allah ﷺ changed their life

60
00:05:33,581 --> 00:05:36,644
and the longer a person would spend with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

61
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:38,749
the more different the character would become.

62
00:05:40,301 --> 00:05:42,722
But now these recruits are new Muslims.

63
00:05:43,824 --> 00:05:46,864
Some of them became Muslim during the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ

64
00:05:46,884 --> 00:05:51,231
but many of them have only met Rasool Allah ﷺ very briefly.

65
00:05:51,255 --> 00:05:55,735
See we have this, there are a lot of misnomers that we have about our Islamic history.

66
00:05:56,633 --> 00:06:00,106
And we think that the early Fatoohaat(فتوحات) were all done by the Sahabah(صحابه).

67
00:06:01,079 --> 00:06:03,114
And that's not correct.

68
00:06:03,448 --> 00:06:08,681
I mean, when you look at the number of Sahabah(صحابه) that spent the most time with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

69
00:06:08,705 --> 00:06:10,480
they are Muhajireen(مهاجرين) who were from Makkah.

70
00:06:11,449 --> 00:06:13,110
How many Muhajireen(مهاجرين) do you think, they were.?

71
00:06:14,874 --> 00:06:17,076
The Muslims who embraced Islam in Makkah?

72
00:06:18,021 --> 00:06:23,341
The foundation of Islam, the ones that Rasool Allah ﷺ spent the most time with,

73
00:06:23,436 --> 00:06:24,690
How many were they?

74
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:27,826
A little over 100! That's all.

75
00:06:28,587 --> 00:06:31,111
Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) are a little over a 100.

76
00:06:31,597 --> 00:06:35,707
We're not talking in 1000s but each one of them is equal to an Ummah(امة).

77
00:06:36,554 --> 00:06:40,292
Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار) were more Al-Ansaar(اَلْاَنْصَار) were a few 100.

78
00:06:42,156 --> 00:06:48,335
The Sahabah(صحابه) who were with Rasool Allah ﷺ in Baiyah Tur-Ridhwan(بَيْعة الرضوان) were 1400.

79
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:53,554
The ones, who attended Hajj(حَجْ) with Rasool Allah ﷺ were 90,000

80
00:06:53,865 --> 00:06:58,664
and the number of Sahabah(صحابه) who prayed Janazah(جنازة) on Rasool Allah ﷺ was 124,000.

81
00:06:59,036 --> 00:07:06,247
Now our scholars consider us a Sahabi(صحابي) to be anyone, who saw Rasool Allah ﷺ as a Muslim.

82
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:10,071
Anybody who saw Rasool Allah ﷺ as a Muslim is a Sahabi(صحابي).

83
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:15,403
So all what is needed to qualify as a Sahabi(صحابي)

84
00:07:16,719 --> 00:07:20,003
is to get a glimpse of Rasool Allah ﷺ when you are a Muslim.

85
00:07:20,952 --> 00:07:23,490
Because for example, if a Mushrik(مشرك) sees Rasool Allah ﷺ

86
00:07:23,515 --> 00:07:26,346
and then they become Muslim later, what are they considered?

87
00:07:26,577 --> 00:07:31,279
But anyway, the view is that as long as you saw Rasool Allah ﷺ, even as a child,

88
00:07:31,821 --> 00:07:33,272
you are a Sahabi(صحابي).

89
00:07:34,016 --> 00:07:37,411
So many of these Sahabah(صحابه) didn't really spend a lot of time with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

90
00:07:37,435 --> 00:07:40,476
So the 90,000, who are in Hajja-Tul-Widah(حجة الوداع),

91
00:07:40,554 --> 00:07:44,744
they just met him for Hajj(حَجْ) and then they left, everybody went back to their home.

92
00:07:45,655 --> 00:07:48,313
So it was the people who are in Madina

93
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:52,442
that were affected by the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ the most.

94
00:07:53,476 --> 00:07:56,023
So these new recruits were coming into Madina.

95
00:07:56,908 --> 00:08:02,128
Some of them were rude, some of them were harsh.

96
00:08:03,517 --> 00:08:05,543
So there were some problems going on in Madina and

97
00:08:05,568 --> 00:08:08,778
the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were being patient and they were taking this.

98
00:08:10,785 --> 00:08:15,441
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was sensing the discomfort of the Sahabah(صحابه),

99
00:08:15,465 --> 00:08:20,986
I mean the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم are seeing all of these people coming to Madina with different behavior,

100
00:08:21,255 --> 00:08:26,239
 some of them are unruly, and they haven't gone through the Tarbiah(تربيعة) yet.

101
00:08:27,412 --> 00:08:30,071
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he gathers all of the Sahabah(صحابه).

102
00:08:30,832 --> 00:08:33,873
And he goes on the Mimber(ممبر) and he says,

103
00:08:34,785 --> 00:08:40,001
نشهدتك الله هم راعًى مسلمًا سمع نشتي لما كفى عنها ها أولآ الأقوم

104
00:08:40,337 --> 00:08:44,209
ومن راعى لي عليه حقَا  فليحتمل ضرب السنتهم

105
00:08:44,466 --> 00:08:48,156
وعجلتًا يكرحوها منهم ما يبلغ ذالك الحد

106
00:08:48,402 --> 00:08:56,085
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: I ask you, in the name of Allah to be patient with these people.

107
00:08:57,648 --> 00:09:02,390
 And if their tongues are sharp, not to respond back to them.

108
00:09:03,609 --> 00:09:10,704
And if they abuse any one of you, be patient and don't respond back

109
00:09:11,368 --> 00:09:16,090
as long as what they have done doesn't reach to the level of a Hadd(حدّ), a crime

110
00:09:16,449 --> 00:09:17,696
that is punishable in Shariah(شريعة).

111
00:09:19,458 --> 00:09:23,843
Overlook their mistakes. And then he said:

112
00:09:24,648 --> 00:09:32,909
فَاِنَّ الله مُهلكٌ بها أولآء أعداعُنَا جُموع هراقل والروم وَإنَّمَا هُم إخوانكم

113
00:09:33,194 --> 00:09:37,190
فان كانت منهم عجلا على أحدٍ مِنكم فليحتمل ذالك

114
00:09:37,396 --> 00:09:41,961
ألم يكن ذالك أستغفر في الرايع خيرًا في المعادي من أن ينتصر منهم

115
00:09:42,768 --> 00:09:48,301
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه because these are the men,

116
00:09:48,861 --> 00:09:53,239
whom Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will use to destroy Heraclius and the Romans.

117
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:59,545
So isn't it appropriate for us to be patient and overlook their mistakes?

118
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:00,877
So the Muslim said: Yes,

119
00:10:00,901 --> 00:10:08,855
بلى، قال فانهم اخوانكم في الديني وانصاركم على أعداء ولهم عليكم حقٌ فحتمل ذالك منهم  ثم نزل من الممبر

120
00:10:09,064 --> 00:10:10,156
The Muslim said: Yes!

121
00:10:10,353 --> 00:10:13,793
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said: These are your brothers in religion

122
00:10:14,118 --> 00:10:21,042
and they are your supporters against your enemies and you have some duties towards them

123
00:10:21,119 --> 00:10:22,809
so be patient with them.

124
00:10:24,802 --> 00:10:30,548
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه you can see the wisdom behind this.

125
00:10:31,670 --> 00:10:33,648
These are people who didn't go for Tarbiah(تربيعة) yet,

126
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:40,064
but they are going to be the foundation of the Muslim armies.

127
00:10:40,794 --> 00:10:44,657
The number of the Sahabah(صحابه), as I told you is very few it's very small in number

128
00:10:44,982 --> 00:10:47,860
they are going to fill all of the leadership positions.

129
00:10:48,692 --> 00:10:51,835
But the foot soldiers are all going to be from these recruits

130
00:10:52,481 --> 00:10:54,700
and they haven't been through the Tarbiah(تربيعة) yet.

131
00:10:56,262 --> 00:11:00,450
However, since they are going to be participating in the Daroat Sanamil Islam(دروعة سنامل اسلام),

132
00:11:00,474 --> 00:11:04,510
the highest thing in Islam, which is fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله عزَّوَجل),

133
00:11:04,915 --> 00:11:08,290
therefore, we should overlook their flaws and mistakes.

134
00:11:09,328 --> 00:11:13,285
And this is a Naseeha(نَصيحة) that holds true all the time.

135
00:11:14,612 --> 00:11:23,087
If someone is practicing a very noble deed in Islam and they make some mistakes,

136
00:11:23,703 --> 00:11:25,933
but they are benefiting the Ummah(امة) greatly.

137
00:11:26,852 --> 00:11:32,561
Then one needs to be forgiving with such a person, or people.

138
00:11:33,455 --> 00:11:37,625
Now, especially in the context of War,

139
00:11:38,904 --> 00:11:46,933
soldiers after fighting for a very long time tend to develop some negative attributes.

140
00:11:47,794 --> 00:11:53,647
The hearts could become harsh, a soldier could turn ruthless after a while

141
00:11:55,337 --> 00:11:58,092
and that is something that goes along with fighting,

142
00:11:58,148 --> 00:12:02,768
it is something that happens if a person spends a lot of time in that area.

143
00:12:03,628 --> 00:12:06,882
And many of these recruits were tribal warriors.

144
00:12:07,294 --> 00:12:09,856
I mean, it's not like they just this is the first time they're going to be fight.

145
00:12:10,309 --> 00:12:13,266
I mean, they've been fighting for all of their life.

146
00:12:14,239 --> 00:12:19,032
And these are the people, who tend to respond first to the call of Jihad(جهاد).

147
00:12:19,244 --> 00:12:24,023
So when Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was asking for recruits to come from Yemen?

148
00:12:24,158 --> 00:12:25,524
I mean, who would you expect to come?

149
00:12:26,462 --> 00:12:31,075
The strong man, the fighters would show up while the soft ones, would stay behind.

150
00:12:31,969 --> 00:12:38,960
And the soft ones that tend to be better on the manners side are not going to show up for this.

151
00:12:38,985 --> 00:12:43,497
You're going to have the warriors, who will come and respond to the call of fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

152
00:12:44,391 --> 00:12:48,922
So they tended to have a very harsh character that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم did not like.

153
00:12:49,547 --> 00:12:52,781
I mean the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم represented the perfection.

154
00:12:53,539 --> 00:12:56,088
I mean, they weren't strong in one area and weak in another.

155
00:12:56,619 --> 00:13:04,330
They had the ability to combine between both having Rahma(رحمة) with the believers

156
00:13:04,697 --> 00:13:07,294
and being harsh against the enemies of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

157
00:13:07,350 --> 00:13:09,191
They represented the perfection in that

158
00:13:10,074 --> 00:13:13,016
but now we had all of these new recruits coming into Madina.

159
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:16,442
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is saying: Don't turn them away.!

160
00:13:17,035 --> 00:13:18,514
Don't be strict with them!

161
00:13:19,569 --> 00:13:21,014
Loosen the rules a little bit!

162
00:13:21,498 --> 00:13:23,811
Why? Because we have a greater cause.

163
00:13:25,312 --> 00:13:28,354
Because these are the ones, who will break down

164
00:13:28,671 --> 00:13:31,581
the obstacles of Da'wah(دعوة) in the Roman Empire.

165
00:13:32,187 --> 00:13:35,761
It will be because of them, that Islam will spread to other people.

166
00:13:36,523 --> 00:13:43,002
Give them time! Give them a chance, to mix with you to learn from you and they will change.

167
00:13:43,501 --> 00:13:47,536
Because by accompanying the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم in their armies,

168
00:13:47,853 --> 00:13:53,079
the characters would be modified and those unruly personalities would be tamed.

169
00:13:54,348 --> 00:13:58,113
Therefore, we can also learn from this, is that

170
00:13:58,910 --> 00:14:01,520
with the brothers who are fighting, Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله),

171
00:14:02,708 --> 00:14:06,192
one should protect their honor and one should defend them,

172
00:14:06,958 --> 00:14:08,837
and one should make Dua(دُعَا) for them

173
00:14:09,267 --> 00:14:10,796
and when they make mistakes,

174
00:14:11,111 --> 00:14:14,501
we ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ to forgive them and to show them the straight path

175
00:14:14,526 --> 00:14:16,310
because nobody is perfect.

176
00:14:16,969 --> 00:14:21,273
And we should apply the same rule that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is applying here.

177
00:14:21,883 --> 00:14:24,114
We shouldn't be very critical of them.

178
00:14:26,508 --> 00:14:30,716
Some additional incidents that happened with Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

179
00:14:32,013 --> 00:14:36,422
He once went in Madina to visit a seminary, Jewish seminary,

180
00:14:38,021 --> 00:14:43,352
Madrasa(مدرسة) of Al-Yahood(أليهود) where they would teach their students a Taurah(توراة).

181
00:14:44,117 --> 00:14:45,323
He went there for Da'wah(دعوة).

182
00:14:46,188 --> 00:14:51,823
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه he goes in, to the Madrasa(مدرسة) or seminary,

183
00:14:52,093 --> 00:14:55,471
and there were some Rabbis in there, one of them, his name is Fanhaas(فنحاص).

184
00:14:56,217 --> 00:14:59,567
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he walks in and he says:

185
00:14:59,592 --> 00:15:06,327
ويحك! اتَّق الله، وأسلم، فوالله إنك تعلم: أنَّ محمداً لرسول الله

186
00:15:06,643 --> 00:15:11,556
قد جاءكم بالحقِّ من عنده، تجدونه مكتوباً عندكم في التَّوراة، والإنجيل

187
00:15:12,505 --> 00:15:15,810
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he told Fanhaas(فنحاص), he said;

188
00:15:16,661 --> 00:15:19,031
Woe to you fear Allah and become a Muslim.

189
00:15:19,872 --> 00:15:24,385
Because you know, that Muhammadﷺ is the messenger of Allah.

190
00:15:24,789 --> 00:15:30,905
And he came with the truth from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, and you find it in the Torah(توراة) and in the Gospel.

191
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:36,546
Fanhaas(فنحاص), he responded by saying, In the name of Allah O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

192
00:15:37,010 --> 00:15:44,549
we do not need Allah, but Allah needs us and we do not pray to Allah but He prays to us,

193
00:15:45,317 --> 00:15:47,159
and we are rich and He is poor.

194
00:15:47,979 --> 00:15:57,166
And if Allah was rich, He would not ask us to give money in charity as your Prophet claims.

195
00:15:58,563 --> 00:16:04,404
 He tells you not to pay Riba(ربا) and then He gives it to us.

196
00:16:05,357 --> 00:16:10,216
If Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ was rich, He would not give us Riba(ربا).

197
00:16:11,234 --> 00:16:15,234
Fanhaas(فنحاص) was being sarcastic, he's saying;

198
00:16:15,742 --> 00:16:20,292
Muhammadﷺ is asking you to give charity, which is an indication that your God is poor.

199
00:16:21,390 --> 00:16:25,097
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he became angry obviously.

200
00:16:26,529 --> 00:16:29,134
So he started beating the face of Fanhaas(فنحاص),

201
00:16:29,303 --> 00:16:31,570
فضرب وجه فنحاص ضرباً شديداً

202
00:16:31,594 --> 00:16:35,974
He was hitting him in his face, until he injured him so then

203
00:16:36,482 --> 00:16:38,920
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه after he beat him up. He said:

204
00:16:39,312 --> 00:16:44,521
In the name of Allah if it wasn't because we have a treaty, I would have killed you.

205
00:16:45,539 --> 00:16:48,119
So Fanhaas(فنحاص), he went to Muhammadﷺ to complain.

206
00:16:48,594 --> 00:16:52,554
And he said to Rasool Allah ﷺ, Look at what your friend has done to me.

207
00:16:53,108 --> 00:16:54,560
So Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

208
00:16:54,584 --> 00:16:56,028
ما حملك على ما صنعت؟

209
00:16:56,116 --> 00:16:58,626
O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) why did you do, what you did?

210
00:16:59,119 --> 00:17:00,985
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

211
00:17:01,210 --> 00:17:03,951
The enemy of Allah has said something great,

212
00:17:04,201 --> 00:17:07,329
he claims that Allah is poor and that they are rich.

213
00:17:07,702 --> 00:17:11,288
And when he said that I became very angry and that's why I beat him up.

214
00:17:12,191 --> 00:17:18,790
Fanhaas(فنحاص), he lied and he didn't admit that he made that statement. And he said:

215
00:17:18,822 --> 00:17:19,770
"ما قلت ذلك"

216
00:17:19,810 --> 00:17:21,032
 I did not say that.

217
00:17:21,452 --> 00:17:24,595
So Fanhaas(فنحاص), he lied.

218
00:17:25,114 --> 00:17:33,254
So Qur'an, the Ayah(آية) of Qur'an came down in Surat-Al Imran(سورة ألعمران) Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says in verse 181.

219
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:38,490
لَقَدْ سَمِعَ اللَّهُ قَوْلَ الَّذِينَ قَالُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ فَقِيرٌ وَنَحْنُ أَغْنِيَاءُ

220
00:17:38,862 --> 00:17:44,415
سَنَكْتُبُ مَا قَالُوا وَقَتْلَهُمُ الأَنْبِيَاءَ بِغَيْرِ حَقٍّ وَنَقُولُ ذُوقُوا عَذَابَ الْحَرِيقِ۝

221
00:17:44,823 --> 00:17:48,347
Allah has certainly heard the statement of those Jews, who said;

222
00:17:48,635 --> 00:17:53,323
Indeed Allah is poor, while we are rich, we will record what they said

223
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:55,858
and their killing of the prophets without right

224
00:17:56,108 --> 00:17:59,743
and will say taste the punishment of the burning fire.

225
00:18:00,928 --> 00:18:07,118
So the Qur'an came to agree with what Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said about the man.

226
00:18:09,409 --> 00:18:15,801
So, I mean, in Da'wah(دعوة), the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم would sometimes get into conflicts,

227
00:18:15,826 --> 00:18:18,279
I mean a lot of these incidents would happen in Makkah and

228
00:18:18,686 --> 00:18:21,487
a few of these incidents also happened in Madina.

229
00:18:22,131 --> 00:18:30,121
I mean, they would give our politely but they would not accept any abuse, or Sabk(سبك) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

230
00:18:30,169 --> 00:18:35,861
they would not accept such statements against Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ or Muhammadﷺ.

231
00:18:37,742 --> 00:18:43,936
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had great fear from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ in terms of the Khauf(خوف).

232
00:18:44,836 --> 00:18:47,852
Muhammad Ibn Sireen(محمدإبن سيرين) he's one of the Taba'een(تابعين), he says:

233
00:18:48,249 --> 00:18:52,666
لم يكن احد أحي بما يعلم بعد النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم من ابي بكر

234
00:18:52,983 --> 00:18:57,397
There was no one who had more fear after Rasool Allah ﷺ than Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

235
00:18:58,046 --> 00:19:03,448
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in terms of Khashiyah(خشية) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, fear of Allah

236
00:19:03,488 --> 00:19:07,091
 and by the way, fear of Allah is the fruit of knowledge.

237
00:19:07,836 --> 00:19:08,749
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

238
00:19:08,790 --> 00:19:10,820
إِنَّمَا يَخْشَى اللَّهَ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ الْعُلَمَاءُ

239
00:19:11,394 --> 00:19:14,820
The ones, who fear Allah are who? The scholars,

240
00:19:15,199 --> 00:19:20,439
therefore, knowledge should lead the person to having fear of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ.

241
00:19:20,918 --> 00:19:24,376
If a person is knowledgeable and they do not fear Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

242
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:26,541
then they have not benefited from their knowledge.

243
00:19:28,545 --> 00:19:30,504
So fear of Allah is the fruit of knowledge.

244
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:37,543
So when Imam Ahmad Ibn Hanbal(إمام أحمد إبن حنبل) heard someone speak about one of the contemporaries, of his.

245
00:19:37,856 --> 00:19:38,650
He said;

246
00:19:39,211 --> 00:19:41,593
He doesn't have any Ilm(علم), he's an ignorant man.

247
00:19:42,415 --> 00:19:45,864
 Imam Ahmad Ibn Hanbal(إمام أحمد إبن حنبل) said: He has the fruit of knowledge,

248
00:19:45,888 --> 00:19:47,421
خشيت الله عزَّوَجل

249
00:19:47,878 --> 00:19:49,799
Meaning, Yes, the man doesn't have a lot of knowledge

250
00:19:49,824 --> 00:19:52,198
but he has the fruit of knowledge, which is the fear of Allah.

251
00:19:52,550 --> 00:19:57,914
So he already has the result of knowledge and that is the fear of Allah Ta'la(تعالى).

252
00:19:58,857 --> 00:20:03,582
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه has so much fear of Allah, that he would sometimes say,

253
00:20:04,458 --> 00:20:09,354
والله لودت أنِّيْ كنت هذه شَجَرَةٌ  تُؤْكَلُ و تُعْضَدُ

254
00:20:09,783 --> 00:20:12,982
I wish that I was this tree, it is eaten and cut down.

255
00:20:13,877 --> 00:20:17,302
Sometimes he would wish that he would be a tree

256
00:20:18,319 --> 00:20:23,073
that is cut down and eaten and that's the end of it.

257
00:20:23,303 --> 00:20:26,038
So there is no reckoning on the day of judgment for it.

258
00:20:26,905 --> 00:20:31,744
And that is because of his fear of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, he used to fear Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ so much,

259
00:20:32,337 --> 00:20:35,071
even though he was at that high status.

260
00:20:36,563 --> 00:20:41,679
In terms of Eeman(ايمان), he had the greatest Eeman(ايمان) of the Ummah(امة),

261
00:20:41,822 --> 00:20:46,235
one of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, he saw a dream.

262
00:20:47,035 --> 00:20:51,009
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

263
00:20:51,034 --> 00:20:52,464
هل راة أحدكم منكم رُؤْيَا

264
00:20:52,488 --> 00:20:55,917
Did anyone of you see a dream? So this man said: Yes!

265
00:20:55,956 --> 00:20:58,117
O Messenger of Allah, I did see a dream.

266
00:20:58,566 --> 00:21:02,663
I saw that there was a scale that came down from the sky.

267
00:21:03,145 --> 00:21:06,879
And then you were placed on one side of the scale,

268
00:21:07,223 --> 00:21:09,834
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was placed on the other side of the scale.

269
00:21:10,043 --> 00:21:13,485
So you were heavier than Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

270
00:21:14,579 --> 00:21:18,391
And then Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was placed on one side and Umar(عُمَر) on the other

271
00:21:18,587 --> 00:21:20,839
and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was heavier than Umar(عُمَر)

272
00:21:21,331 --> 00:21:25,430
and then Umar(عُمَر) was placed on one side and Uthman(عثمان) was placed on the other

273
00:21:26,504 --> 00:21:29,183
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was heavier than Uthman(عثمان).

274
00:21:30,165 --> 00:21:36,829
When Rasool Allah ﷺ heard that dream, he didn't like it. And he said:

275
00:21:36,984 --> 00:21:40,317
خلافة النبوة ثم يؤتي الله الملك من يشاء

276
00:21:40,972 --> 00:21:45,288
It will be Khilafah(خِلَافَه) on the path of Prophethood and then it will be kingdom

277
00:21:45,995 --> 00:21:48,554
because Rasool Allah ﷺ interpreted the dream to mean

278
00:21:48,886 --> 00:21:51,240
that the time of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) after him will be short

279
00:21:51,873 --> 00:21:53,830
and then after that, it will turn into kingdom.

280
00:21:54,287 --> 00:21:58,463
So it's first Rasool Allah ﷺ, and then Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and then Umar(عُمَر) and then Uthman(عثمان).

281
00:21:58,725 --> 00:22:03,268
And then by the time Ali(علي) becomes Khalifah(خليفه), the Fitten(فتن) would have started.

282
00:22:05,675 --> 00:22:10,843
His Eeman(ايمان) there's another Hadith(حديث) and this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

283
00:22:11,903 --> 00:22:16,364
Rasool Allah ﷺ, after Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاة الفجر), he would talk to the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

284
00:22:16,389 --> 00:22:22,487
like conversation you know, they will talk about dreams, he would give them reminders

285
00:22:22,776 --> 00:22:27,492
they would discuss in one narration it says, that the Sahabah(صحابه) would joke.

286
00:22:27,870 --> 00:22:30,996
And Rasool Allah ﷺ would be sitting quiet but he would smile.

287
00:22:32,824 --> 00:22:36,501
So, one day Rasool Allah ﷺ turns around after the Salah(صلاة) and he says:

288
00:22:37,902 --> 00:22:46,912
بيْنَا رَجُلٌ يَسُوقُ بَقَرَةً قد حمل عليها ، فالْتَفَتَت إليه البقرةُ، فقالَت: إنِّي لم أخْلَقْ لِهَذا ولكن خُلُقتُ لِلْحَرْثِ

289
00:22:47,813 --> 00:22:55,938
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: One day a man was with his cow, so he mounted his cow.

290
00:22:57,731 --> 00:23:03,968
So the cow told him: I was not created for this, I was created for tilling the land.

291
00:23:05,515 --> 00:23:06,955
So the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم said;

292
00:23:07,027 --> 00:23:09,261
سُبحانَ اللهِ! بَقرةٌ تَتَكلَّمُ،

293
00:23:09,757 --> 00:23:11,870
Glory be to Allah, a cow is speaking.

294
00:23:12,788 --> 00:23:17,476
So this is what turned the attention of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, How can a cow speak?

295
00:23:18,590 --> 00:23:20,048
What did the Rasool Allah ﷺ say?

296
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:21,847
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

297
00:23:21,934 --> 00:23:25,580
فإنِّي أُومِنُ بهذا أنَا، وأَبُو بَكْرٍ، وعُمَرُ

298
00:23:26,164 --> 00:23:33,640
I believe in this and so does Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) and then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

299
00:23:35,031 --> 00:23:41,450
And one day a wolf took away a goat from a shepherd.

300
00:23:42,049 --> 00:23:47,239
So the shepherd pursued the wolf, until he released his goat from him.

301
00:23:47,410 --> 00:23:49,540
So the wolf turns around and says;

302
00:23:49,815 --> 00:23:54,288
هذا اسْتَنْقَذْتَهَا مِنِّي، فمَن لَهَا يَومَ السَّبُعِ، يَومَ لا رَاعِيَ لَهَا غيرِي؟

303
00:23:55,155 --> 00:23:57,556
You were able to release this goat from me

304
00:23:57,718 --> 00:24:04,458
but what will you do in the day of the beasts when the sheep will have no shepherd but me.?

305
00:24:04,890 --> 00:24:09,996
So the wolf is saying a time will come when the goats and the sheep

306
00:24:10,020 --> 00:24:13,250
will have no shepherd around but us, the wolves.

307
00:24:13,877 --> 00:24:15,004
So the Sahabah(صحابه) again said;

308
00:24:15,028 --> 00:24:16,868
سُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ! ذِئْبٌ يَتَكَلَّمُ،

309
00:24:17,021 --> 00:24:21,466
Glory to Allah, a wolf is speaking. Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

310
00:24:22,349 --> 00:24:25,412
فإنِّي أُومِنُ بهذا أنَا، وأَبُو بَكْرٍ، وعُمَرُ

311
00:24:25,666 --> 00:24:29,181
I believe in this, me, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

312
00:24:29,518 --> 00:24:31,655
Abu Hurayrah(أبوهريرة) who's narrating the Hadith(حديث), he said:

313
00:24:31,924 --> 00:24:33,134
 "وما هُما ثَمَّ"

314
00:24:33,307 --> 00:24:36,340
And Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) weren't even present.

315
00:24:38,505 --> 00:24:40,568
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) weren't present

316
00:24:41,394 --> 00:24:46,300
 nevertheless Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that me and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) believe in this.

317
00:24:46,639 --> 00:24:48,702
So Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling the Sahabah(صحابه)

318
00:24:48,952 --> 00:24:53,775
that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) believe in everything that I say even if they don't know it.

319
00:24:54,648 --> 00:24:59,144
Even if they're not present, they still have in belief everything that I say.

320
00:24:59,432 --> 00:25:01,168
So their Eeman(ايمان) is so high,

321
00:25:01,645 --> 00:25:05,283
they don't even need evidences for what I say they believe in it.

322
00:25:06,135 --> 00:25:09,454
And this is a very important attribute for Al-Mo'min(ألمؤمن).

323
00:25:10,506 --> 00:25:12,591
Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ describes Al-Muttaqeen(ألمتقين)

324
00:25:13,327 --> 00:25:17,029
and the first quality Allah gives to Al-Muttaqeen(ألمتقين) in Surat-Ul-Baqarah(سورة البقرة) is what?

325
00:25:17,342 --> 00:25:23,135
الم۝ذَلِكَ الْكِتَابُ لَا رَيْبَ فِيهِ هُدًى لِلْمُتَّقِينَ۝الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ

326
00:25:23,808 --> 00:25:27,139
Al-Muttaqeen(ألمتقين), the first quality they believe in the unseen.

327
00:25:28,339 --> 00:25:30,998
So, the element of belief is very important

328
00:25:32,633 --> 00:25:38,430
that you believe in whatever Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says and whatever Muhammadﷺ says or does.

329
00:25:40,170 --> 00:25:45,457
You know, it doesn't have to be verified through an empirical experiment.

330
00:25:46,273 --> 00:25:51,696
It doesn't have to be confirmed by other people around you, whom you respect.

331
00:25:52,703 --> 00:25:57,197
Because why am I saying this, in this context?

332
00:25:57,689 --> 00:26:03,382
Sometimes our environment enforces upon us certain concepts,

333
00:26:05,202 --> 00:26:09,881
the media, the people around us, we might hear it even from scholars.

334
00:26:10,452 --> 00:26:12,317
So we take these things for granted.

335
00:26:13,475 --> 00:26:17,032
So then when we find that a Hadith(حديث) or an Ayah(آية) contradicts

336
00:26:17,102 --> 00:26:19,018
this concept that we have in our mind,

337
00:26:19,495 --> 00:26:21,314
we don't go with the literal meaning of the Hadith(حديث).

338
00:26:21,354 --> 00:26:27,065
No we change the meaning to confirm with our concept and that's not the right way.

339
00:26:27,513 --> 00:26:28,496
The right way is,

340
00:26:28,536 --> 00:26:35,674
 if the Ayah(آية) or the Hadith(حديث) presents a concept in a certain way you adopt it, even if it is against

341
00:26:36,259 --> 00:26:38,110
what the environment around you is telling you.

342
00:26:38,772 --> 00:26:41,947
And I think that by going through the story of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

343
00:26:42,759 --> 00:26:46,542
you would find that many of the concepts that you have

344
00:26:46,614 --> 00:26:50,161
or people around you have turned out to be misnomers.

345
00:26:50,201 --> 00:26:53,563
I mean, when you look at the understanding that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had,

346
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:59,431
in terms of Da'wah(دعوة), in terms of war, in terms of the role of Khalifah(خليفه),

347
00:26:59,696 --> 00:27:01,895
in terms of the priority of Muslims

348
00:27:02,165 --> 00:27:06,482
it is quite different than what is the accepted norm in our time.

349
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:11,224
And the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم according to what we have went through have done things

350
00:27:11,349 --> 00:27:16,804
that are unacceptable according to modern concepts.

351
00:27:16,915 --> 00:27:19,012
So which are you going to adopt?

352
00:27:21,342 --> 00:27:27,463
And that's why we find that there's a lot of missed interpretation  of Ayaat(آيات) and Ahadith(احاديث) going on.

353
00:27:27,809 --> 00:27:28,408
Why?

354
00:27:28,590 --> 00:27:35,837
The sole purpose of that is to make it conform with the acceptable norms of the day

355
00:27:35,951 --> 00:27:38,951
and thus not the right way to go about it.

356
00:27:39,904 --> 00:27:42,646
The right thing is what Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) did,

357
00:27:43,615 --> 00:27:47,431
that was the right way, and the only right way.

358
00:27:48,998 --> 00:27:56,643
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه he has the greatest Eeman(ايمان) of this Ummah(امة).

359
00:27:57,230 --> 00:27:59,124
لشيءٍ وكرة في قلبه

360
00:27:59,558 --> 00:28:03,091
There was something that was mentioned in one narration

361
00:28:03,721 --> 00:28:06,618
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is special because of something that's settled in his heart.

362
00:28:07,246 --> 00:28:13,448
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was the most beloved to Rasool Ullah صلوات الله والسلام عليه.

363
00:28:13,481 --> 00:28:18,296
Amr Bin Al-Aas رضي الله عنه, he said: I went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and I asked him

364
00:28:18,321 --> 00:28:19,854
this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

365
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:24,655
He says: I asked Rasool Allah ﷺ who's the most beloved person to you?

366
00:28:25,109 --> 00:28:27,785
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Ayesha(عائشه), my wife.

367
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:32,425
Ayesha(عائشه), she is the most beloved person to me, he used to love her so much.

368
00:28:34,097 --> 00:28:36,957
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص), he said: What about from amongst the men?

369
00:28:38,280 --> 00:28:39,831
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Her father.

370
00:28:41,147 --> 00:28:45,692
So out of the women, it's Ayesha(عائشه), out of the men her father, such a blessed family.

371
00:28:46,352 --> 00:28:49,090
The family of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

372
00:28:50,634 --> 00:28:56,844
In another Hadith(حديث) Rasool Allah ﷺ says: And this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

373
00:28:57,495 --> 00:28:58,586
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

374
00:28:58,611 --> 00:29:04,122
Whoever is a person of Salah(صلاة) will be invited from the gate of Salah(صلاة) in Jannah(جنة).

375
00:29:04,752 --> 00:29:09,327
And whoever is a person of fasting will be invited from the gate of Ar-Rayyan(ألريان),

376
00:29:09,561 --> 00:29:14,194
which is for the ones, who fast and whoever was from the people of Jihad(جهاد)

377
00:29:14,232 --> 00:29:16,163
will be called from the gate of Jihad(جهاد),

378
00:29:16,565 --> 00:29:20,504
and whoever is from the people of Sadaqah(صدقه) will be called from the gate of Sadaqah(صدقه).

379
00:29:21,835 --> 00:29:23,093
What did Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) asked?

380
00:29:23,896 --> 00:29:27,278
He said: Well, there'll be somebody who's invited from all of these gates.

381
00:29:28,062 --> 00:29:32,884
So the aspiration of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was not just to get through from one gate, but

382
00:29:34,643 --> 00:29:39,445
he was looking at getting an invitation from each of the eight gates of Jannah(جنة).

383
00:29:39,470 --> 00:29:41,974
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes! And you are one of them.

384
00:29:43,021 --> 00:29:49,178
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is going to be one of the exclusive group,

385
00:29:49,217 --> 00:29:51,845
who will be invited from every gate of Jannah(جنة).

386
00:29:51,885 --> 00:29:56,508
See you can imagine the gatekeepers of Jannah(جنة), who are the gatekeepers Jannah(جنة)? Malaikah(ملائكه)!

387
00:29:57,194 --> 00:30:01,413
And every one of them is trying to convince Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to enter from his gate,

388
00:30:01,954 --> 00:30:04,255
and they're all competing to get his attention

389
00:30:04,595 --> 00:30:07,919
and to get the honor of having him go through their gate.

390
00:30:09,063 --> 00:30:12,224
So the gatekeepers of Jihad(جهاد) come from here, the gatekeepers of Sadaqah(صدقه),

391
00:30:12,248 --> 00:30:14,805
the gatekeepers of Sayyam(صيام), the gatekeepers of Salah(صلاة),

392
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:20,312
they're all trying to pull Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and convince him to go in from their gate.

393
00:30:20,569 --> 00:30:23,968
So Allah Alam(الله أعلم), which gate Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه will choose.

394
00:30:26,635 --> 00:30:29,780
The knowledge of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه. Ibn Taymiyah(اِبْنِ تَيْمِيَّه) says;

395
00:30:29,804 --> 00:30:33,511
وقد أتَّفق أهل السنة على أنَّ أبا بكر أعلم ألأمة

396
00:30:33,935 --> 00:30:38,725
It is the consensus of Ahlus Sunnah(أهل سنة), that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is the most knowledgeable of this Ummah(امة).

397
00:30:39,114 --> 00:30:42,468
 He is the most knowledgeable of this Ummah(امة) and that is because

398
00:30:42,794 --> 00:30:47,325
of the long time exclusive time he has spent with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

399
00:30:47,648 --> 00:30:50,273
You know, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is the only one,

400
00:30:50,306 --> 00:30:54,299
who accompanied the Rasool Allah ﷺ in Al-Hijrah(ألهجرة), which was 11 days long.

401
00:30:54,981 --> 00:30:59,768
So he had exclusive time with Muhammadﷺ, only the two of them.

402
00:31:00,824 --> 00:31:03,844
Only Allah knows what conversation went between them during that time.

403
00:31:04,715 --> 00:31:09,647
And then Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was with Muhammadﷺ from the first day in Makkah.

404
00:31:09,967 --> 00:31:12,475
So he spent the entire 13 years with him.

405
00:31:13,030 --> 00:31:18,123
And then he would spend time alone with Rasool Allah ﷺ because Ayesha(عائشه) says

406
00:31:18,275 --> 00:31:21,100
that he used to visit us every day once or twice.

407
00:31:21,397 --> 00:31:25,029
So on a daily basis, he's meeting with Muhammadﷺ.

408
00:31:25,607 --> 00:31:29,401
And then in Madina, it is reported that at night,

409
00:31:29,740 --> 00:31:33,505
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) would go to the house of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

410
00:31:33,530 --> 00:31:34,392
يسفر عنده

411
00:31:34,834 --> 00:31:38,109
He would spend time at night with Rasool Allah ﷺ alone.

412
00:31:38,498 --> 00:31:41,803
No one else from among the Sahabah(صحابه) is joining them.

413
00:31:42,435 --> 00:31:44,178
And this used to happen very frequently.

414
00:31:44,537 --> 00:31:47,986
So throughout the Da'wah(دعوة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ for 23 years,

415
00:31:48,445 --> 00:31:53,324
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was getting special time with Muhammadﷺ.

416
00:31:54,360 --> 00:31:58,278
So, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) therefore, has heard things from Rasool Allah ﷺ that no one else has heard,

417
00:31:58,786 --> 00:32:02,439
and that makes him the most knowledgeable man in the Ummah(امة)

418
00:32:03,294 --> 00:32:05,521
and you would find out that in many situations,

419
00:32:05,580 --> 00:32:09,340
the Sahabah(صحابه) would end up going back to him, he was their Shaikh(شيخ).

420
00:32:09,643 --> 00:32:12,061
He was the scholar of the Sahabah(صحابه).

421
00:32:12,331 --> 00:32:16,258
So, in the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ it was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر),

422
00:32:16,604 --> 00:32:19,951
who brought them back to the right course.

423
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:24,782
In terms of the burial place of Rasool Allah ﷺ where is he going to be buried?

424
00:32:24,807 --> 00:32:29,241
It was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) told them that Rasool Allah ﷺ should be buried in the place he died.

425
00:32:29,935 --> 00:32:31,885
In terms of the inheritance

426
00:32:32,343 --> 00:32:36,014
I mean, even Fatima(فاطمه), the daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ did not know the rulings about it.

427
00:32:36,427 --> 00:32:39,037
And it was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), who said that Rasool Allah ﷺ said

428
00:32:39,489 --> 00:32:42,231
that the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) don't leave behind an inheritance.

429
00:32:42,256 --> 00:32:46,952
So, you can see that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), had more knowledge

430
00:32:47,327 --> 00:32:50,048
than the direct family members of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

431
00:32:50,759 --> 00:32:52,851
Fatima رضي الله عنها and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب),

432
00:32:53,017 --> 00:32:58,103
even Al-Abbas(العباس) was involved in that, in the Miraas(ميراث) of An-Nabi صلوات الله والسلام عليه.

433
00:32:59,309 --> 00:33:04,596
In the issue of, "ألخلافة في قريش" It was Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), who went to the Ansaar(أنصار)

434
00:33:04,957 --> 00:33:07,599
and told Saad Ibn Ubadah(سعدإبن عبادة) that me and you were present

435
00:33:07,623 --> 00:33:10,201
when Rasool Allah ﷺ said that the leadership is among Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

436
00:33:11,249 --> 00:33:14,272
In the issue of the ones, who did not pay Zakah(زكوة).

437
00:33:15,068 --> 00:33:17,471
All of the Sahabah(صحابه) the issue was not clear to them.

438
00:33:17,772 --> 00:33:19,470
Whether we can fight them or not.

439
00:33:19,620 --> 00:33:23,786
It was Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), who gave them the fatwa(فتوى) on this issue.

440
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:29,454
In the issue of sending out the army of Usama(أسامه), so you can find that he was their reference.

441
00:33:31,881 --> 00:33:35,827
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) also was very knowledgeable in interpreting dreams.

442
00:33:36,959 --> 00:33:40,854
And the issue of dreams you know the Sahabah(صحابه) used to take it seriously.

443
00:33:40,894 --> 00:33:45,575
I mean, we see dreams like we don't see that as a serious thing.

444
00:33:46,760 --> 00:33:53,144
We see it as you know, unreliable and maybe a lot of our dreams are unreliable

445
00:33:53,168 --> 00:33:57,215
because we are living in a time when there's not a lot of truth because for dreams to be true,

446
00:33:57,591 --> 00:33:59,617
أصْدَقُكُم رُؤْيَا أصْدُقكُم حَديثًا

447
00:34:00,278 --> 00:34:04,588
The truest dreams are going to be given to the truest among you, in their speech.

448
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:10,863
So if a person is very deceptive in their character, their dreams will also be deceptive.

449
00:34:11,214 --> 00:34:15,720
But if a person is very straightforward and honest and truthful and trustworthy,

450
00:34:16,142 --> 00:34:19,737
their dreams are going to be exactly like their character.

451
00:34:20,813 --> 00:34:24,293
So the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم used to give weight to dreams

452
00:34:24,318 --> 00:34:26,680
and they would talk about it and they would discuss it.

453
00:34:27,747 --> 00:34:32,287
Rasool Allah ﷺ for example after Salat-Ul-Fajr(صلاةالفجر), like in the Hadith(حديث) that we just mentioned,

454
00:34:32,563 --> 00:34:33,917
هل راة أحدكم منكم رُؤْيَا

455
00:34:33,942 --> 00:34:36,157
He would ask the Sahabah(صحابه), did any one of you see a dream

456
00:34:36,361 --> 00:34:38,443
and then he would interpret the dreams for them.

457
00:34:38,783 --> 00:34:42,493
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه also had the ability to interpret dreams,

458
00:34:43,316 --> 00:34:47,112
once a dream was presented to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

459
00:34:47,382 --> 00:34:48,691
 One of the Sahabah(صحابه) said;

460
00:34:48,863 --> 00:34:57,690
I have seen tonight in my dream, a cloud and dropping from the cloud was honey and butter.

461
00:34:58,623 --> 00:34:59,444
سمن وعسل

462
00:35:00,639 --> 00:35:04,798
And people were taking from this honey and butter.

463
00:35:05,004 --> 00:35:08,147
Some were taking a lot and some were not.

464
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:11,556
And then a rope came down from the heavens.

465
00:35:12,204 --> 00:35:17,726
And you O Messenger of Allah climbed that rope until you disappeared in the heaven.

466
00:35:18,528 --> 00:35:21,432
And then a man after you came and he climbed

467
00:35:22,284 --> 00:35:26,218
and then the rope was cut but then it was connected again.

468
00:35:28,136 --> 00:35:32,510
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he said: O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to interpret it.

469
00:35:34,046 --> 00:35:36,030
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) as we mention before,

470
00:35:36,055 --> 00:35:38,753
he would give Fatwa(فتوى) in the presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ

471
00:35:38,921 --> 00:35:42,620
now he wants to interpret the dream in the in the presence of Rasool Ullah.

472
00:35:43,103 --> 00:35:44,177
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

473
00:35:44,217 --> 00:35:44,752
 "فأعْبُرَهَا"

474
00:35:44,871 --> 00:35:46,155
Go ahead, interpret it.

475
00:35:47,197 --> 00:35:47,889
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said;

476
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:49,352
"أمَّا الظُّلَّةُ فَالإِسْلَامُ"

477
00:35:49,852 --> 00:35:51,918
The cloud represents Islam,

478
00:35:52,463 --> 00:35:55,297
وأَمَّا الذي يَنْطُفُ مِنَ العَسَلِ والسَّمْنِ فَالقُرْآنُ

479
00:35:55,762 --> 00:35:59,070
And the honey and butter that is coming down is Qur'an.

480
00:36:00,465 --> 00:36:04,463
And then the people, who are taking a lot and the people who are not taking so much

481
00:36:05,099 --> 00:36:07,830
 is the benefit that the people are taking from Qur'an

482
00:36:07,855 --> 00:36:11,194
some of them are learning a lot of Qur'an and benefiting from a lot,

483
00:36:11,350 --> 00:36:14,576
while some others are taking less of a quantity of it.

484
00:36:15,587 --> 00:36:19,323
So Qur'an is the honey and butter, it's the Barakah(بركة), it's the blessing.

485
00:36:19,978 --> 00:36:22,966
And then the rope that you climbed,

486
00:36:23,298 --> 00:36:27,007
means that you, O Messenger of Allah will be elevated in status

487
00:36:27,550 --> 00:36:31,035
and then somebody will come after you and they will be elevated in status

488
00:36:31,059 --> 00:36:34,472
and then somebody will come after that person and it will be elevated in the status.

489
00:36:35,120 --> 00:36:36,794
So that was the interpretation of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

490
00:36:37,201 --> 00:36:41,884
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is asking the Messenger of Allah, did I interpret it right?

491
00:36:42,678 --> 00:36:46,484
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Part of it was right and part of it was wrong.

492
00:36:47,076 --> 00:36:49,620
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: In the name of Allah tell me what was wrong.

493
00:36:49,860 --> 00:36:51,852
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "لا تُقْسِمْ" Do not swear.

494
00:36:52,665 --> 00:36:55,526
And he refused to tell him what part was wrong.

495
00:36:57,241 --> 00:37:04,825
Ayesha رضي الله عنها, she said, that she saw a dream where three moons fell down in her house.

496
00:37:05,403 --> 00:37:08,748
Three moons descended in her room.

497
00:37:08,970 --> 00:37:10,835
Actually, we say it's a house but it's a room.

498
00:37:10,875 --> 00:37:13,442
That's all what Ayesha رضي الله عنها had.

499
00:37:13,918 --> 00:37:17,339
Every wife, I mean Ummahaat-Ul-Momineen(أمهَات المؤمنين) would have one room.

500
00:37:17,672 --> 00:37:18,417
That was it!

501
00:37:19,050 --> 00:37:21,199
No kitchen, no restroom.

502
00:37:21,548 --> 00:37:27,206
Qadha Ul-Haja(قضاء الحاجة) was, they would go outside of Madina to respond to the call of nature.

503
00:37:28,857 --> 00:37:30,222
 So their houses were very simple.

504
00:37:31,484 --> 00:37:35,493
So she saw three moons falling in her house.

505
00:37:35,684 --> 00:37:39,067
She went to her father and she said: What's the interpretation of this dream?

506
00:37:39,184 --> 00:37:41,587
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said;

507
00:37:42,387 --> 00:37:49,013
If your dream is true, it means the three greatest men on the face of the earth,

508
00:37:49,515 --> 00:37:52,073
will be buried in your house, in your room.

509
00:37:53,226 --> 00:37:56,821
When Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) told Ayesha(عائشه),

510
00:37:56,970 --> 00:37:58,525
"هذا خيرٌ أبمالق"

511
00:37:58,660 --> 00:38:01,041
 This is the best of your three moons.

512
00:38:01,509 --> 00:38:06,308
Now, to show you the interest that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) gave to dreams.

513
00:38:07,497 --> 00:38:10,254
Ayesha(عائشه) told Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) this dream a long time ago.

514
00:38:10,926 --> 00:38:14,580
But he remembered it and when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away he said;

515
00:38:15,114 --> 00:38:18,083
This is the beginning of the interpretation of your dream.

516
00:38:19,503 --> 00:38:21,257
 In fact, Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) said;

517
00:38:22,324 --> 00:38:27,706
لَئن يَرى رجلٌ مسلم مسبغ الوضؤ الرؤيا صالحة احب ألينا من كذا وكذا

518
00:38:28,355 --> 00:38:34,091
For a Muslim man, who has complete Wudhoo(وضؤ), he is in Taharah(طهارة)

519
00:38:35,082 --> 00:38:38,249
and sees a dream is better to me than this in that.

520
00:38:38,777 --> 00:38:40,483
"كذا وكذا" In Arabic means that,

521
00:38:40,751 --> 00:38:42,878
when you say it's better than Kaza-Wakazaa(كذاوكذا)

522
00:38:42,941 --> 00:38:47,307
it means it's very valuable to me and it's more worth than a lot of things.

523
00:38:47,712 --> 00:38:50,007
 So he valued dreams so much he said that

524
00:38:50,261 --> 00:38:53,946
for a Muslim man, Yusbighul Wudhoo(يسبغ الوضؤ) has Taharah(طهارة)

525
00:38:53,985 --> 00:38:57,013
because also going to bed on Taharah(طهارة)

526
00:38:57,584 --> 00:39:02,961
because when you see a dream and you have Taharah(طهارة) is more of an indication that it's a true dream.

527
00:39:03,833 --> 00:39:05,022
And he also said;

528
00:39:05,046 --> 00:39:07,191
من راة رويَا الصالحة فليحدثنا بها

529
00:39:07,215 --> 00:39:12,088
If you see a good dream then let us know about it, tell us about it.

530
00:39:13,897 --> 00:39:20,267
He would go to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he would ask him to teach him Dua(دُعَا) in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم).

531
00:39:20,564 --> 00:39:23,140
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه he went to Rasool Ullah and said;

532
00:39:23,165 --> 00:39:25,107
عَلِّمْنِي دُعَاءً أدْعُو به في صَلَاتِي،

533
00:39:25,131 --> 00:39:28,713
O Messenger of Allah teach me a Dua(دُعَا) that I can make in my Salah(صلاة).

534
00:39:29,070 --> 00:39:30,982
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to say;

535
00:39:31,789 --> 00:39:34,986
اللَّهُمَّ إنِّي ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِي ظُلْمًا كَثِيرًا،

536
00:39:35,351 --> 00:39:41,074
ولَا يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ إلَّا أنْتَ، فَاغْفِرْ لي مَغْفِرَةً مِن عِندِكَ، وارْحَمْنِي إنَّكَ أنْتَ الغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ

537
00:39:41,338 --> 00:39:44,772
O Allah! I have committed wrong against myself.

538
00:39:44,836 --> 00:39:48,294
I have committed a lot of wrong against myself,

539
00:39:48,745 --> 00:39:53,503
and no one forgives sins but You so forgive me

540
00:39:54,170 --> 00:39:59,810
 and have mercy on me because you are the Forgiving and Merciful, the admission of sin.

541
00:40:02,462 --> 00:40:06,083
If you look at the Dua(دُعَا) of Yunus(يونس) in the stomach of the whale, what did it start with?

542
00:40:07,072 --> 00:40:07,909
He says;

543
00:40:08,216 --> 00:40:10,890
"لا إله إلا أنت سبحانك إني كنت من الظالمين"

544
00:40:11,322 --> 00:40:14,478
O Allah there is no god but You, glory be to You.

545
00:40:15,310 --> 00:40:16,866
I've committed wrong against myself.

546
00:40:16,898 --> 00:40:20,366
So admission of sin is something that Allah likes,

547
00:40:20,509 --> 00:40:25,184
for you to humble yourself and to admit that you have committed mistakes,

548
00:40:25,334 --> 00:40:28,309
and then you ask Allah for forgiveness, that something that Allah loves.

549
00:40:29,226 --> 00:40:34,462
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: If the people stop sinning, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ will create people, who sin

550
00:40:34,804 --> 00:40:38,349
so that they will ask Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ for forgiveness and He will forgive them.

551
00:40:39,004 --> 00:40:42,383
Alright, some other general issues

552
00:40:43,962 --> 00:40:48,428
regarding the Da'wah(دعوة) and Jihad(جهاد) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

553
00:40:50,313 --> 00:40:52,586
Why did the Muslims win against their opponents?

554
00:40:53,318 --> 00:41:01,257
How come Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and his people defeated the enemies of Allah,

555
00:41:01,787 --> 00:41:03,487
the two superpowers of the time?

556
00:41:05,118 --> 00:41:10,690
How were they able to turn around so swiftly within a little over two years

557
00:41:11,358 --> 00:41:16,363
and destroy all opponents of Tauheed(توحيد) in Arabia,

558
00:41:16,803 --> 00:41:22,835
and then start spreading the message to Persia, Iraq and Roman Empire.

559
00:41:24,401 --> 00:41:31,018
Well, the Romans were sending spies to mix within the Muslims.

560
00:41:32,507 --> 00:41:36,983
And they would send Arabs to do that because they had within their territory,

561
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:40,680
the tribes of Ghassan(غسان) and Lakham(لخم).

562
00:41:41,394 --> 00:41:44,485
So these were Arabs living under Roman rule.

563
00:41:45,744 --> 00:41:48,469
So they would hire some of them, to spy for them,

564
00:41:49,205 --> 00:41:51,698
because they could go unnoticed, they speak the language.

565
00:41:52,783 --> 00:41:57,500
So they would go and mix among the Muslim armies and come and report back to them.

566
00:41:58,735 --> 00:42:01,841
And then they would study their reports or their Orientalist give them

567
00:42:01,954 --> 00:42:05,445
the interpretation of the views of the Muslims.

568
00:42:06,205 --> 00:42:07,767
Because it was a new phenomena for them.

569
00:42:07,792 --> 00:42:11,295
It was something that was different than anything they've seen before.

570
00:42:12,486 --> 00:42:16,322
So one of these spies, went back and reported to them

571
00:42:17,836 --> 00:42:22,262
after spending some time among the army of Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد).

572
00:42:23,708 --> 00:42:30,796
He went back and said: These are people, who pray at night and fast during the day.

573
00:42:31,978 --> 00:42:37,645
And if the son of their leader would steal, they would cut their hand

574
00:42:39,032 --> 00:42:44,451
and if any one of them high or low would commit a crime, they would be punished.

575
00:42:46,048 --> 00:42:52,425
So these are Ubbad(عُبَّاد) spend their life worshipping Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ night and day

576
00:42:53,089 --> 00:42:54,831
and they have established justice.

577
00:42:57,308 --> 00:43:04,504
When the army came back from Al-Yarmook(أليرموك), dragging their tails of defeat,

578
00:43:05,646 --> 00:43:07,267
and they met with Heracul(هراقل)

579
00:43:07,481 --> 00:43:10,847
and Heracul(هراقل) has lost his brother, Theodore in that battle.

580
00:43:11,633 --> 00:43:13,617
He said, Waihakum(وَيْحَكُم) Woe to you.

581
00:43:15,013 --> 00:43:18,291
Aren't these men like you? They said: Yes!

582
00:43:18,860 --> 00:43:21,696
Are you more or they are more? They said: We are more.

583
00:43:22,751 --> 00:43:25,710
So he said: How come you are losing? And how come they are winning?

584
00:43:26,375 --> 00:43:29,762
These were the words or the answer that they gave to Heracul(هراقل).

585
00:43:30,657 --> 00:43:32,256
فقال شيخ من عظمائهم

586
00:43:32,281 --> 00:43:33,793
 One of their elders said;

587
00:43:35,290 --> 00:43:37,408
من أجل أنهم يقومون بالليل ،

588
00:43:37,479 --> 00:43:40,115
ويصومون بالنهار، ويوفون بالعهد،

589
00:43:40,155 --> 00:43:44,140
ويأمرون بالمعروف وينهون عن المنكر، ويتناصفون بينهم

590
00:43:44,418 --> 00:43:48,434
، ومن أجل أنا نشرب الخمر ونزني ونركب الحرام

591
00:43:48,644 --> 00:43:51,374
وننقض العهد ونغصب ونظلم

592
00:43:51,466 --> 00:43:54,850
ونأمر بما يسخط الله وننهي عما يرضي الله،

593
00:43:55,032 --> 00:43:56,261
ونفسد في الأرض. قال: أنت صدقتني

594
00:43:56,581 --> 00:44:02,468
He said: The reason, why they're winning and we are losing is because they pray at night

595
00:44:02,760 --> 00:44:06,956
and they fast during the day and they fulfill their covenants

596
00:44:06,981 --> 00:44:12,146
and they enjoined good and they prevent evil and they are just among themselves.

597
00:44:12,482 --> 00:44:16,442
And because we drink alcohol, and we commit adultery and fornication

598
00:44:16,701 --> 00:44:19,862
and we commit every sin and we betray our promises,

599
00:44:19,913 --> 00:44:23,082
and we oppress and we commit wrong and transgression

600
00:44:23,443 --> 00:44:29,697
and because we encourage evil and we prevent people from doing what pleases Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

601
00:44:29,916 --> 00:44:31,564
and because we corrupt in the land.

602
00:44:32,779 --> 00:44:34,667
Heracul(هراقل) said: You're telling me the truth.

603
00:44:36,356 --> 00:44:40,739
Unless the Muslims go back to what the Sahabah(صحابه) were doing,

604
00:44:41,146 --> 00:44:44,798
the situation of our Ummah(امة) will not change.

605
00:44:45,201 --> 00:44:50,210
And as another description was given to a Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

606
00:44:50,562 --> 00:44:53,637
كانو رهبان في اليل فرسان في النهار

607
00:44:54,284 --> 00:44:59,752
They were fighters during the day and monks during the night.

608
00:45:01,668 --> 00:45:11,262
Finally, a few questions to ask, what was the purpose of fighting in the time of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه?

609
00:45:11,924 --> 00:45:13,637
How did they make Da'wah(دعوة)?

610
00:45:15,307 --> 00:45:19,754
What were the rules for accepting soldiers in their armies?

611
00:45:20,908 --> 00:45:26,279
In terms of the purpose of fighting that was understood by Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه

612
00:45:26,908 --> 00:45:31,618
can be learned from the letter that he sent

613
00:45:32,217 --> 00:45:36,198
to the people of Yemen recruiting them to Jihad(جهاد)? He said;

614
00:45:36,952 --> 00:45:43,262
ولا يذال الجهاد لأهل عداوة حتى يدين بدين الحق و يكرُّ الْحُكم الكتاب

615
00:45:43,571 --> 00:45:47,891
He says: Jihad(جهاد) should continue against the enemies of Allah,

616
00:45:47,916 --> 00:45:53,273
until they follow the religion of Allah, and they accept the rule of the book of Allah.

617
00:45:54,010 --> 00:46:00,115
Now, doesn't this seem to contradict our understanding of the Ayah(آية),

618
00:46:00,140 --> 00:46:01,353
"لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ"

619
00:46:01,633 --> 00:46:03,212
There is no compulsion in religion.

620
00:46:03,884 --> 00:46:06,888
Doesn't this seem to contradict our understanding of the Ayah(آية).

621
00:46:06,912 --> 00:46:09,088
أَفَأَنتَ تُكْرِهُ ٱلنَّاسَ حَتَّىٰ يَكُونُواْ مُؤْمِنِينَ

622
00:46:09,345 --> 00:46:13,393
When Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is telling Muhammadﷺ are you going to compel people to become believers?

623
00:46:13,962 --> 00:46:19,098
How can we combine between the words of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), not only his words, but his actions too.

624
00:46:19,457 --> 00:46:22,201
I mean look at how he treated Al-Murtaddeen(مرتدين) in Arabia,

625
00:46:22,496 --> 00:46:26,472
and then look at how he attacked the Roman Empire and the Persian Empire.

626
00:46:27,381 --> 00:46:29,985
The Roman Empire and the Persian Empire did not invade Madina.

627
00:46:31,998 --> 00:46:34,647
We could say maybe they had conspiracies to do so.

628
00:46:35,905 --> 00:46:38,751
But the most we can say is that this was a preemptive strike.

629
00:46:38,775 --> 00:46:43,884
We cannot say that this was a defensive Jihad(جهاد) per se.

630
00:46:44,604 --> 00:46:51,237
It was clearly an offensive Jihad(جهاد), Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is sending an army to Iraq,

631
00:46:51,363 --> 00:46:53,132
he is sending an army into Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

632
00:46:55,029 --> 00:46:59,955
And he's sending letters to the Heracul(هراقل) and to his generals

633
00:46:59,976 --> 00:47:04,918
and he's sending a letter to Kisra(كسرى) telling them become a Muslim or pay Jizya(جزية).

634
00:47:06,374 --> 00:47:10,014
So in some cases, it seems that the war that was initiated

635
00:47:10,061 --> 00:47:13,459
by Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and then later Umar(عُمَر) was unprovoked.

636
00:47:16,040 --> 00:47:21,828
So how can we understand that in light of our perception of what Jihad(جهاد) is?

637
00:47:23,720 --> 00:47:25,298
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث),

638
00:47:25,361 --> 00:47:29,769
أُمِرْتُ أَن أُقاتِلَ النَّاسَ حَتَّى يَشْهَدُوا أَن لا إِلهَ إِلاَّ اللَّه وأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ

639
00:47:30,785 --> 00:47:35,341
I was commanded to fight the people, until they testify that there's no God but Allah,

640
00:47:35,621 --> 00:47:38,215
and that Muhammadﷺ is the Messenger of Allah.

641
00:47:39,008 --> 00:47:44,784
This Hadith(حديث), is Mutawatit(متواتر), which is the highest level of strength in Hadith(حديث),

642
00:47:45,539 --> 00:47:50,823
it was narrated by Bukhari(بخاريْ), Muslim(مسلم), Darqutni(دارقطني), Tabraani(طبراني), Al-Hakim(ألحاكم),

643
00:47:51,252 --> 00:47:56,726
and An-Nasae(ألنسائ), Abu Dawood(ابوداؤد), At-Tirmadhi(الترمذي) and it was narrated by over 12

644
00:47:56,751 --> 00:47:59,569
of the Sahabah(صحابه), Abu Huraira رضي الله عنه, Anas Ibn Malik(أنس إبن مالك),

645
00:47:59,594 --> 00:48:04,103
Jarir Ibn Abdullah(جرير إبن عبدالله), An-Noman Ibn Bashir(نعمان إبن بشير) and others.

646
00:48:04,637 --> 00:48:09,167
When we say Mutawatit(متواتر) it means that the Hadith(حديث) is certainly authentic.

647
00:48:09,214 --> 00:48:10,807
It's the highest level of Sahih(صحيح),

648
00:48:10,989 --> 00:48:13,727
Sahih(صحيح) has levels of Mutawatit(متواتر) and Ahaat(أحات).

649
00:48:13,926 --> 00:48:15,031
This is the strongest.

650
00:48:16,348 --> 00:48:24,765
So when you want to understand the concept you have to gather all of the text that was mentioned for that issue.

651
00:48:25,765 --> 00:48:26,548
So you have the Ayah(آية)

652
00:48:26,573 --> 00:48:27,540
لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي الدِّينِ

653
00:48:27,825 --> 00:48:28,473
And the Ayah(آية)

654
00:48:28,513 --> 00:48:30,362
"أَفَأَنتَ تُكْرِهُ ٱلنَّاسَ حَتَّىٰ يَكُونُواْ مُؤْمِنِينَ"

655
00:48:30,408 --> 00:48:31,517
And then you have the Hadith(حديث),

656
00:48:31,557 --> 00:48:32,469
 "أُمِرْتُ أَن أُقاتِلَ النَّاسَ"

657
00:48:32,493 --> 00:48:33,907
I was commanded to fight the people.

658
00:48:34,383 --> 00:48:36,113
So how can you combine between the two.

659
00:48:37,407 --> 00:48:38,796
Ibn Hajar(إبن حجَر) says

660
00:48:39,511 --> 00:48:44,796
 after mentioning a few different interpretations of the meaning of the Hadith(حديث), he says,

661
00:48:46,039 --> 00:48:48,218
one of the meanings is that,

662
00:48:48,584 --> 00:48:53,273
Rasool Allah ﷺ and whoever takes his position after him the Khalifah(خليفه)

663
00:48:54,290 --> 00:48:58,790
should fight the people, until they either become Muslim

664
00:48:59,618 --> 00:49:03,528
or they accept the Hukum(حكم) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

665
00:49:03,634 --> 00:49:08,888
the rule of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, the rule of Qur'an which in this case is Jizya(جزية).

666
00:49:09,833 --> 00:49:13,473
In other words, the purpose of fighting Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

667
00:49:14,076 --> 00:49:18,077
is to eliminate any opposition to the rule of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

668
00:49:18,149 --> 00:49:22,746
and to make the people either accept the religion and adopt it.

669
00:49:23,672 --> 00:49:27,797
Or at least they accept the dominance of law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

670
00:49:27,821 --> 00:49:31,023
and then they follow whatever religion they want, after they have accepted

671
00:49:31,325 --> 00:49:33,593
the fact that the law of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is dominant.

672
00:49:34,020 --> 00:49:38,698
So what is meant by the Ayah(آية) is that you cannot force individuals

673
00:49:39,101 --> 00:49:43,179
to adopt the religion, cannot bring a person and tell him you must become a Muslim.

674
00:49:43,306 --> 00:49:44,306
No.

675
00:49:45,282 --> 00:49:49,016
You make them accept the fact that the earth belongs to Allah

676
00:49:49,041 --> 00:49:51,410
and the law of Allah needs to be applied on Earth.

677
00:49:52,111 --> 00:49:57,038
But then after that, they have the freedom to choose whichever belief they want to believe in.

678
00:49:57,746 --> 00:50:04,478
So what Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was doing was falling under the these, this definition of Jihad(جهاد),

679
00:50:04,503 --> 00:50:08,394
so he was fighting against the Romans and the Persians to eliminate,

680
00:50:08,698 --> 00:50:11,629
it was eliminated the governance of Kuffr(كفر) on land,

681
00:50:12,125 --> 00:50:18,529
but then, many people in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام) continued practicing Christianity and Judaism

682
00:50:18,554 --> 00:50:24,816
and that's why we have Christians in Syria, Falastine(فلسطين), Jordan, Lebanon, and Iraq.

683
00:50:25,741 --> 00:50:28,550
I mean, if they were forced to accept Islam,

684
00:50:29,161 --> 00:50:32,930
you wouldn't have any religious minorities in these countries.

685
00:50:33,396 --> 00:50:41,461
So after 1400 years of Islam in these countries, these religious minorities survived,

686
00:50:42,031 --> 00:50:43,270
but they were Ahluz-Zimmah(أهل الذمة).

687
00:50:43,365 --> 00:50:49,001
And Ahluz-Zimmah(أهل الذمة) accepted the fact that the law of Allah will apply on their land

688
00:50:49,814 --> 00:50:52,004
and that they have to pay the Jizya(جزية) to the Muslims.

689
00:50:54,141 --> 00:50:55,740
What was their method of Da'wah(دعوة)?

690
00:50:55,842 --> 00:51:00,135
Did Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه send the letter to Heraclius

691
00:51:00,639 --> 00:51:04,817
asking him permission for the Sahabah(صحابه) to go and distribute leaflets

692
00:51:05,244 --> 00:51:09,713
in Damascus and Jerusalem and we want to present the Da'wah(دعوة) to the people.?

693
00:51:10,190 --> 00:51:11,074
Did he do that?

694
00:51:12,316 --> 00:51:16,262
Did the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم go and present the Da'wah(دعوة) to each and every one

695
00:51:16,293 --> 00:51:19,485
of the people in the Roman Empire before they fought them.

696
00:51:19,768 --> 00:51:20,709
The answer is no.

697
00:51:21,705 --> 00:51:24,627
The Da'wah(دعوة) that Rasool Allah ﷺ would give and the Sahabah(صحابه)

698
00:51:24,652 --> 00:51:26,245
is Da'wah(دعوة) to the leaders of the people.

699
00:51:26,817 --> 00:51:30,418
They wouldn't go down to the masses, they would go straight to the leadership.

700
00:51:31,068 --> 00:51:34,138
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not send letters to each and every citizen

701
00:51:34,655 --> 00:51:38,565
of the Persian Empire and the Roman Empire or to the Arab tribes.

702
00:51:38,858 --> 00:51:40,404
He would go and speak to the leadership.

703
00:51:41,194 --> 00:51:43,934
When he spoke to the people of At-Taef(اَلطَّائِف), he went and spoke to their leaders,

704
00:51:44,610 --> 00:51:47,702
when they would go and talk to the tribes in Al-Hajj(ألحَجْ),

705
00:51:47,782 --> 00:51:49,188
he would go and speak to the leadership.

706
00:51:49,213 --> 00:51:52,711
He wouldn't go to each and every individual asking them to become Muslim.

707
00:51:53,204 --> 00:51:57,692
He would go to the leaders and speak to them directly or he would send them letters.

708
00:51:58,395 --> 00:52:02,617
The acceptance of the leader is taken as acceptance of everyone

709
00:52:02,903 --> 00:52:08,140
and the rejection of the leader is taken as rejection of everyone and therefore war is justified.

710
00:52:09,140 --> 00:52:13,028
So when Heracul(هراقل) turned down the invitation of Islam,

711
00:52:14,061 --> 00:52:17,735
the Muslims had the right to fight all the people

712
00:52:18,658 --> 00:52:22,370
and they were all targets of the Jihad(جهاد) of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

713
00:52:22,751 --> 00:52:26,540
When Kisra(كسرى) tore the letter of Rasool Allah ﷺ

714
00:52:27,338 --> 00:52:30,218
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه sent armies to fight

715
00:52:30,765 --> 00:52:33,848
even though the masses of the people did not hear the Da'wah(دعوة) of Islam.

716
00:52:34,977 --> 00:52:39,387
So this was the method of the Da'wah(دعوة) of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

717
00:52:39,680 --> 00:52:40,477
Third issue.

718
00:52:41,149 --> 00:52:43,493
We have this perception and I'm trying to deal with the misnomers,

719
00:52:43,533 --> 00:52:44,824
we have this perception

720
00:52:45,211 --> 00:52:49,134
that fighting is later stage that should only occur

721
00:52:49,411 --> 00:52:52,233
after a person has went through Jihad An-Nafs(جهادأنفس) and preparation.

722
00:52:52,989 --> 00:52:56,638
So there's a lot of preparation that needs to take place before

723
00:52:56,958 --> 00:52:59,550
somebody can participate in fighting in Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

724
00:53:00,740 --> 00:53:07,389
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he was in Madina, when somebody would come to him and accept Islam,

725
00:53:08,085 --> 00:53:11,753
he would immediately send them out in the armies.

